---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import {
  ChatConfirmationPlayground,
  ChatConfirmationReminder,
  ChatConfirmationStates,
  ChatConfirmationTableApproval,
} from "../../components/ChatConfirmationDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Chat Confirmation"
  description="Asks someone in chat to approve or decline an action an agent proposed, with the facts, a submitting state, and the outcome."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Chat Confirmation</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Asks someone in chat to approve or decline an action an agent proposed. It
    is a <a href="/components/review-card/">Review Card</a> with a shield icon, a
    status badge, the facts as rows, and two buttons. Once decided it folds and shows
    the outcome.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><ChatConfirmationPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A table change waiting for approval"
      code={`import {
  ChatConfirmation,
  type ConfirmationState,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/chat-confirmation";

const [state, setState] = useState<ConfirmationState>({ kind: "pending" });

<ChatConfirmation
  title="Remove the Notes field from Supplier deliveries"
  description="Review these changes before approving."
  details={[
    { label: "Action", value: "Change table schema" },
    { label: "Effect", value: "Remove field values" },
    { label: "Affected rows", value: "128" },
  ]}
  state={state}
  disabled={!canVerifyEffect}
  onDecision={async (decision) => {
    setState({ kind: "submitting", decision });
    setState(await save(decision));
  }}
/>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>title</code>: what the agent wants to do. Long titles end with an
        ellipsis.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>description</code>: one line above the facts.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>details</code>: <code>{"{ label, value }[]"}</code>, shown in
        order. Long values wrap.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>state</code>: <code>pending</code>,
        <code>{'{ kind: "submitting", decision }'}</code>,
        <code>approved</code>, <code>rejected</code>, <code>expired</code>,
        <code>cancelled</code>, or
        <code>{'{ kind: "error", message }'}</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>onDecision</code>: called with <code>"approve"</code> or
        <code>"reject"</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>disabled</code>: locks both buttons, such as while the request is
        refreshing or its effect cannot be verified.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>approveLabel</code>: names the action on the approve button, such
        as “Approve 3 drafts”. Defaults to “Approve action”.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      Pending, submitting, and error show <strong>Approval required</strong>
      with both buttons. While submitting, both are disabled and the chosen one shows
      a spinner. An error shows above the buttons so people can try again. Approved,
      declined, expired, and cancelled fold the card and show the outcome.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><ChatConfirmationStates client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Table approval in chat</h2>
    <p>
      A schema change with its request status below: details, a status check,
      and an alert when the refresh failed. The buttons lock while the request
      needs a check and when the effect cannot be verified.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><ChatConfirmationTableApproval client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Settle without submitting</h2>
    <p>
      A decision can settle at once. Pick any state from the menu. This one
      names its action with <code>approveLabel="Send reminder"</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4"><ChatConfirmationReminder client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The card is a <code>section</code> named by the title, which is an
      <code>h4</code> button that opens and closes the details. A busy button has
      <code>aria-busy</code> and its spinner is hidden. Errors use
      <code>role="alert"</code>; the outcome uses <code>role="status"</code>. If
      the decision was made from inside the card, focus moves to the outcome
      when it settles, so keyboard users keep their place.
    </p>
    <p>
      The details grow and shrink in 180ms; with reduced motion they change at
      once.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Text uses <code>--sprout-muted</code>, errors
      <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and the outcome focus ring
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>. The card, badge, and buttons use their own
      tokens.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
